# /etc/personal_settings_popup_disabled - Puppy skips its first-run Quick Setup when this file exists.
#
# Cycle 17 item 9. /usr/sbin/delayedrun runs quicksetup once per fresh data partition and its questions are
# desktop questions the appliance answers for itself: /etc/keymap is us, /etc/localtime is the owner's zone, and
# /etc/hostname is 1bit-os. On the cycle-16 board recording the wizard did not appear and the clock still read
# UTC, so the wizard's absence and the missing timezone were both accidental. Nothing about the wizard is wanted
# on a demo box, so the switch Puppy itself provides is thrown here.
